literal_statement:
Let $q=p^h$ be a prime power and let $m(k-1;q)$ denote the maximum length of a $q$-ary MDS code of dimension $k$ (equivalently, the maximum size of an arc in $\mathrm{PG}(k-1;q)$). For $q>k-1$, the Main Conjecture asserts
\[
m(k-1;q)=
\begin{cases}
q+2, & \text{if $q$ is even and }(k=3\text{ or }k=q-1),\\
q+1, & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\]
